'\" t
.TH "ACTON\-SIMULATED\-LOCALNET" "1"
.nh
.ad l
.ss \n[.ss] 0
.SH "NAME"
acton\-simulated\-localnet \[em] Run Acton\[cq]s simplified TON development environment
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
\fBacton simulated\-localnet\fR [\fIoptions\fR] \fIcommand\fR
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Acton simulated localnet is a fast, deterministic TON development environment
for local execution, forked\-state development, and faucet\-based funding. It
produces TON\-compatible blocks and provides LiteAPI, TON Center v2/v3, Streaming
API, and Emulate API surfaces used by many contract and dApp workflows.
.sp
It is Acton\[cq]s custom simplified implementation, not a real TON network or
validator cluster. It does not model validators, consensus, shard elections,
or the full production node and indexer stack.
.SH "SUBCOMMANDS"
.SS "acton simulated-localnet start"
Start Acton\[cq]s simplified TON development environment.
.SS "Synopsis"
\fBacton simulated\-localnet start\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
.SS "Options"
.sp
\fB\-\-port\fR \fIport\fR
.RS 4
Simulated localnet HTTP port.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-fork\-net\fR \fInetwork\fR
.RS 4
Remote network to use for forked account resolution.
.sp
The fork also uses the network configuration from the resolved masterchain
block. With an explicit historical block, it uses that block\[cq]s Unix time;
otherwise, the virtual clock starts from the current system Unix time.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-fork\-block\-number\fR \fIseqno\fR
.RS 4
Historical block sequence number to fork from.
.sp
The selected block provides the local network configuration and virtual\-clock
origin.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-accounts\fR \fIname\fR[,\fIname\fR\[u2026]]_
.RS 4
Project wallets to initialize and fund with 100 GRAM. Defaults to \fB[localnet].accounts\fR\&.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-db\-path\fR \fIpath\fR
.RS 4
Path to a SQLite database for persistent node state. Defaults to
\fB[localnet].db\-path\fR when configured.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-rate\-limit\fR \fIrps\fR
.RS 4
Maximum \fB/api\fR requests per second to simulate provider rate limits.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-response\-delay\-ms\fR \fIms\fR
.RS 4
Delay TON Center v2/v3 and Emulate API responses.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-block\-time\-ms\fR \fIms\fR
.RS 4
Target interval between automatic blocks, in milliseconds. Ignored when
automatic mining is disabled.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-no\-mining\fR
.RS 4
Disable automatic block production. Mine blocks manually with
\fBacton simulated\-localnet mine\fR or \fBPOST /acton_mine\fR\&.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-snapshots\-dir\fR \fIpath\fR
.RS 4
Directory for persistent JSON snapshots. Defaults to a \fB\&.snapshots\fR directory
next to the SQLite database, or \fB\&.acton/simulated\-localnet/<port>/snapshots\fR
inside the project when no database is configured.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-liteapi\fR
.RS 4
Start the LiteAPI server on the TCP port immediately after the Localnet HTTP
port. LiteAPI is disabled by default.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-liteapi\-port\fR \fIport\fR
.RS 4
Set the LiteAPI TCP port explicitly. Requires \fB\-\-liteapi\fR; otherwise LiteAPI
uses the Localnet HTTP port plus one.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-require\-auth\fR
.RS 4
Require a token for all Localnet HTTP API, control, emulate, and streaming
endpoints. The server prints the token on startup.
.RE
.SS "acton simulated-localnet airdrop"
Send GRAM from the local faucet to an address.
.SS "Synopsis"
\fBacton simulated\-localnet airdrop\fR [\fIoptions\fR] \fIaddress\fR
.SS "Options"
.sp
\fIaddress\fR
.RS 4
Recipient address.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-a\fR, \fB\-\-amount\fR \fIgram\fR
.RS 4
Amount of GRAM to request.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-port\fR \fIport\fR
.RS 4
Simulated localnet HTTP port.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-auth\-token\fR \fItoken\fR
.RS 4
Localnet API token for a server started with \fB\-\-require\-auth\fR\&. If omitted,
Acton reads \fBACTON_LOCALNET_AUTH_TOKEN\fR\&.
.RE
.SS "acton simulated-localnet mine"
Mine localnet blocks manually.
.SS "Synopsis"
\fBacton simulated\-localnet mine\fR [\fIoptions\fR] [\fIn\fR]
.SS "Options"
.sp
\fIn\fR
.RS 4
Number of blocks to mine. Defaults to \fB1\fR\&.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-port\fR \fIport\fR
.RS 4
Simulated localnet HTTP port.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-auth\-token\fR \fItoken\fR
.RS 4
Localnet API token for a server started with \fB\-\-require\-auth\fR\&. If omitted,
Acton reads \fBACTON_LOCALNET_AUTH_TOKEN\fR\&.
.RE
.SS "acton simulated-localnet increase-time"
Increase the localnet virtual clock.
.SS "Synopsis"
\fBacton simulated\-localnet increase\-time\fR [\fIoptions\fR] \fIseconds\fR
.SS "Options"
.sp
\fIseconds\fR
.RS 4
Seconds to add to the virtual localnet clock.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-port\fR \fIport\fR
.RS 4
Simulated localnet HTTP port.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-auth\-token\fR \fItoken\fR
.RS 4
Localnet API token for a server started with \fB\-\-require\-auth\fR\&. If omitted,
Acton reads \fBACTON_LOCALNET_AUTH_TOKEN\fR\&.
.RE
.SS "acton simulated-localnet set-time"
Set the localnet virtual clock.
.SS "Synopsis"
\fBacton simulated\-localnet set\-time\fR [\fIoptions\fR] \fItimestamp\fR
.SS "Options"
.sp
\fItimestamp\fR
.RS 4
Unix timestamp in seconds. The timestamp cannot be lower than the latest mined
block time.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-port\fR \fIport\fR
.RS 4
Simulated localnet HTTP port.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-auth\-token\fR \fItoken\fR
.RS 4
Localnet API token for a server started with \fB\-\-require\-auth\fR\&. If omitted,
Acton reads \fBACTON_LOCALNET_AUTH_TOKEN\fR\&.
.RE
.SS "acton simulated-localnet set-next-block-timestamp"
Set a one\-shot timestamp for the next localnet block.
.SS "Synopsis"
\fBacton simulated\-localnet set\-next\-block\-timestamp\fR [\fIoptions\fR] \fItimestamp\fR
.SS "Options"
.sp
\fItimestamp\fR
.RS 4
Unix timestamp in seconds for the next mined block. The timestamp is consumed
by the next automatic or manually mined block and cannot be lower than the
latest mined block time.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-port\fR \fIport\fR
.RS 4
Simulated localnet HTTP port.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-auth\-token\fR \fItoken\fR
.RS 4
Localnet API token for a server started with \fB\-\-require\-auth\fR\&. If omitted,
Acton reads \fBACTON_LOCALNET_AUTH_TOKEN\fR\&.
.RE
.SS "acton simulated-localnet status"
Inspect the current localnet status.
.SS "Synopsis"
\fBacton simulated\-localnet status\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
.SS "Options"
.sp
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-port\fR \fIport\fR
.RS 4
Simulated localnet HTTP port.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-json\fR
.RS 4
Print machine\-readable JSON.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-auth\-token\fR \fItoken\fR
.RS 4
Localnet API token for a server started with \fB\-\-require\-auth\fR\&. If omitted,
Acton reads \fBACTON_LOCALNET_AUTH_TOKEN\fR\&.
.RE
.SS "acton simulated-localnet snapshot"
Save and restore persistent JSON snapshots of a localnet.
.SS "Synopsis"
\fBacton simulated\-localnet snapshot\fR [\fIoptions\fR] \fIcommand\fR
.SS "Subcommands"
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fBcreate [name]\fR saves the current network state
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fBlist\fR prints saved snapshots with IDs, names, block seqnos, and file sizes
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fBrestore <id>\fR restores the saved network state
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fBdelete <id>\fR deletes one saved snapshot
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fBexport <id> \-\-out <path>\fR downloads a saved snapshot; \fB\-\-force\fR replaces an existing file
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fBimport <path> [\-\-name <name>]\fR validates and saves a JSON snapshot under a new ID without restoring it
.RE
.sp
Snapshots survive node restarts. Creation and restoration run in the node\[cq]s
mutation queue without stopping its process. A snapshot includes accounts,
block and transaction history, registered metadata, pending messages, and
virtual time. Restoration also updates SQLite when persistence is enabled.
.sp
Relative file paths resolve from the Acton project root. These commands call the
running localnet control API. Pass \fB\-\-port\fR or \fB\-\-auth\-token\fR when needed, and
\fB\-\-json\fR for structured output. Use the returned ID for restore, delete, and export.
.SH "CONFIGURATION"
You can store defaults in \fBActon.toml\fR:
.sp
.RS 4
.nf
[localnet]
port = 5411
db\-path = ".acton/localnet.sqlite"
fork\-net = "testnet"
fork\-block\-number = 55000000
accounts = ["deployer", "user"]
rate\-limit = 1
response\-delay\-ms = 300
block\-time\-ms = 500
no\-mining = false
.fi
.RE
.sp
CLI flags override config values for the current invocation. In particular,
\fB\-\-db\-path\fR overrides \fB[localnet].db\-path\fR\&. A relative path in \fBActon.toml\fR
resolves from the project root, while a relative \fB\-\-db\-path\fR resolves from the
current working directory.
.SH "TON CENTER API KEYS"
When localnet forks from the built\-in \fBmainnet\fR/\fBtestnet\fR backends,
authenticated requests read \fBTONCENTER_MAINNET_API_KEY\fR or
\fBTONCENTER_TESTNET_API_KEY\fR\&.
.sp
When localnet forks from \fBcustom:<name>\fR, Acton reads
\fB<NORMALIZED_NAME>_API_KEY\fR\&. Custom network names are uppercased and
non\-alphanumeric characters are replaced with \fB_\fR, so \fBcustom:mock\-remote\fR
becomes \fBMOCK_REMOTE_API_KEY\fR\&.
.sp
Acton loads \fB\&.env\fR automatically, so the simplest setup during project work is
usually to keep these keys there and use shell environment variables only for
one\-off overrides or CI.
.SH "LOCALNET API AUTH"
\fBacton simulated\-localnet start \-\-require\-auth\fR protects every Localnet HTTP route under
\fB/api/*\fR, \fB/acton_*\fR, \fB/api/emulate/*\fR, and \fB/api/streaming/*\fR\&. Static UI files
remain public, but the bundled UI does not receive the token from the server.
When a protected API request returns \fB401\fR, the bundled UI shows a token overlay;
paste the printed token there before using protected API views. The key button
in the sidebar footer reopens the same overlay.
.sp
When auth is enabled, the server prints a localnet API token. Pass it as either:
.sp
.RS 4
.nf
Authorization: Bearer <TOKEN>
X\-API\-Key: <TOKEN>
.fi
.RE
.sp
\fBAuthorization: Bearer\fR is the preferred form. \fBX\-API\-Key\fR is accepted for
TON Center\-compatible clients. Browser WebSocket clients can pass \fBtoken=<TOKEN>\fR
only on \fB/api/streaming/v2/ws\fR\&.
.sp
For CLI subcommands that call localnet control routes, pass \fB\-\-auth\-token\fR or
set \fBACTON_LOCALNET_AUTH_TOKEN\fR\&. If \fBACTON_LOCALNET_AUTH_TOKEN\fR is set when
starting with \fB\-\-require\-auth\fR, localnet uses that value; otherwise it generates
and prints a fresh token.
.SH "RUNTIME MODEL"
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'fork mode allows local development against remote chain state
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fBacton simulated\-localnet start\fR runs in the foreground until the process is stopped
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'Acton starts an HTTP server on \fB127.0.0.1:<port>\fR for localnet API, control
endpoints, and the bundled localnet UI
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'the server keeps running until the process is stopped, for example with
\fBCtrl+C\fR
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'the Localnet UI is available on the root path, for example
\fBhttp://127.0.0.1:<port>/\fR
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'the node produces a block every \fB\-\-block\-time\-ms\fR milliseconds, defaults
to 500 ms, and still creates empty blocks when no transactions are queued
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fB\-\-no\-mining\fR or \fB[localnet].no\-mining = true\fR disables automatic block
production; use \fBacton simulated\-localnet mine [N]\fR or \fBPOST /acton_mine\fR to create
blocks manually
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'localnet has a virtual clock for block and transaction time; use
\fBacton simulated\-localnet increase\-time\fR, \fBacton simulated\-localnet set\-time\fR, or
\fBacton simulated\-localnet set\-next\-block\-timestamp\fR to move it without waiting for real
time
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'messages accepted through \fBsend_boc\fR, \fBacton_sendInternalMessage\fR, or the
faucet are queued and included on a later automatic or manually mined block
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'a block can include multiple transactions; locally generated internal
messages are processed in the same block when possible
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'the bundled UI is a single\-page explorer app, so routes like \fB/explorer\fR,
\fB/tokens\fR, \fB/nfts\fR, and per\-address or per\-transaction pages are served from
the same frontend shell
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'the UI reads chain data from \fB/api/v2\fR and \fB/api/v3\fR, and uses \fBacton_*\fR
control endpoints for local address aliases, registered compiler ABIs,
status and saved snapshots
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fB\-\-require\-auth\fR protects read and write API routes, including read\-only
streaming endpoints
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'when \fB\-\-port\fR and \fB[localnet].port\fR are both absent, the current runtime
fallback is \fB5411\fR
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fB\-\-rate\-limit\fR applies to \fB/api/*\fR endpoints, not admin endpoints
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fB\-\-response\-delay\-ms\fR applies only to \fB/api/v2\fR, \fB/api/v3\fR, and
\fB/api/emulate/v1\fR endpoints; streaming, control, and UI routes are not
delayed
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fBPOST /acton_setNetworkConditions\fR can change the response delay while the
server is running, and \fBGET /acton_nodeInfo\fR reports the current value
.RE
.SH "CONTROL ENDPOINTS"
The localnet server exposes \fBacton_*\fR control routes for local development
tooling:
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fBGET /acton_nodeInfo\fR returns uptime, latest block seqno, and the active state
source
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fBPOST /acton_createSnapshot\fR with \fB{"name":"before\-upgrade"}\fR saves a JSON snapshot
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fBGET /acton_listSnapshots\fR lists saved snapshots
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fBPOST /acton_restoreSnapshot\fR with \fB{"id":"<SNAPSHOT_ID>"}\fR restores the saved network state
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fBPOST /acton_deleteSnapshot\fR with \fB{"id":"<SNAPSHOT_ID>"}\fR deletes one saved file
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fBGET /acton_exportSnapshot?id=<SNAPSHOT_ID>\fR downloads the saved JSON file
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fBPOST /acton_importSnapshot?name=bug\fR validates JSON bytes and saves them under
a new ID without changing the running state
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fBPOST /acton_setConfig\fR with \fB{"config":"<BASE64_BOC>"}\fR validates and
replaces the full blockchain config dictionary, then commits it in a
config\-only block
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fBPOST /acton_setConfigParam\fR with
\fB{"index":2,"boc":"<BASE64_BOC>","expectedHash":"<CURRENT_CELL_HASH>"}\fR
replaces one config parameter and commits a config\-only block, even when
automatic mining is disabled. \fBexpectedHash\fR is the current parameter\[cq]s
lowercase hexadecimal representation hash; use \fBnull\fR to add a missing
parameter. A stale hash returns HTTP 409. Parameter 0 cannot be changed
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fBPOST /acton_setShardAccount\fR with
\fB{"address":"<ADDR>","shard_account":"<BASE64_BOC>"}\fR replaces the selected
account state with a base64\-encoded \fBShardAccount\fR BOC
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fBPOST /acton_sendInternalMessage\fR with \fB{"boc":"<BASE64_BOC>"}\fR sends a
base64\-encoded internal message BOC through the local internal queue
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fBPOST /acton_mine\fR with optional \fB{"blocks":N}\fR mines queued and/or empty
blocks manually; \fBN\fR defaults to \fB1\fR
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fBPOST /acton_increaseTime\fR with \fB{"seconds":3600}\fR adds seconds to the
virtual localnet clock
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fBPOST /acton_setTime\fR with \fB{"timestamp":1710000000}\fR sets the current
virtual Unix time
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fBPOST /acton_setNextBlockTimestamp\fR with \fB{"timestamp":1710000600}\fR sets a
one\-shot timestamp for the next mined block
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fBPOST /acton_setNetworkConditions\fR with \fB{"response_delay_ms":300}\fR updates
simulated network latency; use \fB0\fR to disable response delay
.RE
.sp
Acton Studio exposes the same parameter editor under \fBConfig\fR in the
\fBNetwork\fR section for simulated localnet environments. Changes preserve all
other parameters and historical configs.
.sp
TON Center\-compatible message endpoints such as \fB/api/v2/sendBoc\fR and
\fB/api/v3/message\fR accept external\-in messages only. Use
\fB/acton_sendInternalMessage\fR when local tooling needs to inject a raw internal
message.
.sp
Control endpoints are unauthenticated by default for local development. Use
\fB\-\-require\-auth\fR when another local process, browser page, or test harness should
not be able to read or mutate the running localnet without the token. Do not
expose the localnet server publicly.
.SH "PERSISTENCE"
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fB\-\-db\-path\fR or \fB[localnet].db\-path\fR enables persistent SQLite\-backed node
state across runs
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fBsnapshot create\fR saves a persistent restore point as JSON
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fB\-\-snapshots\-dir\fR sets the directory used for saved snapshots
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'blockchain configs changed through \fB/acton_setConfig\fR or
\fB/acton_setConfigParam\fR are stored in block history and survive restarts when
\fB\-\-db\-path\fR is configured
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'without a database, live state is ephemeral; saved snapshots remain available
in the snapshot directory
.RE
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fB0\fR: The selected localnet subcommand completed successfully. For
\fBacton simulated\-localnet status\fR, this also includes the selected port not running;
use \fB\-\-json\fR and inspect \fBrunning\fR for automation.
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fB1\fR: Startup failed because port binding, database setup, remote fork
initialization, faucet handling, or a status/control query failed.
.RE
.SH "DISPLAY OPTIONS"
.sp
\fB\-\-color\fR \fIwhen\fR
.RS 4
Control when to use colored output.
.sp
Possible values: \fBauto\fR, \fBalways\fR, \fBnever\fR
.RE
.SH "PROJECT OPTIONS"
.sp
\fB\-\-manifest\-path\fR \fIpath\fR
.RS 4
Path to the \fBActon.toml\fR file to use for this invocation.
.sp
Use this when running the command outside the project directory or when the
manifest lives at a non\-default location.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-project\-root\fR \fIpath\fR
.RS 4
Path to the project root to use for configuration discovery and relative
defaults.
.sp
This conflicts with \fB\-\-manifest\-path\fR\&.
.RE
.SH "EXAMPLES"
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04' 1.\h'+01'Start with defaults:
.sp
.RS 4
.nf
acton simulated\-localnet start
.fi
.RE
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04' 2.\h'+01'Fork from testnet at a historical block:
.sp
.RS 4
.nf
acton simulated\-localnet start \-\-fork\-net testnet \-\-fork\-block\-number 55000000
.fi
.RE
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04' 3.\h'+01'Use a dedicated snapshot directory:
.sp
.RS 4
.nf
acton simulated\-localnet start \-\-snapshots\-dir snapshots
.fi
.RE
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04' 4.\h'+01'Airdrop local funds:
.sp
.RS 4
.nf
acton simulated\-localnet airdrop UQA_ftKIJsHEAE_UgtFOUK15hPzycZooFuUr8duyY9T3kwwM \-\-amount 25
.fi
.RE
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04' 5.\h'+01'Start a local integration node with pre\-funded accounts:
.sp
.RS 4
.nf
acton simulated\-localnet start \-\-accounts deployer,user \-\-db\-path build/localnet.db
.fi
.RE
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04' 6.\h'+01'Inspect a running localnet:
.sp
.RS 4
.nf
acton simulated\-localnet status \-\-json
.fi
.RE
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04' 7.\h'+01'Save and share a snapshot:
.sp
.RS 4
.nf
acton simulated\-localnet snapshot create before\-upgrade
acton simulated\-localnet snapshot list \-\-json
acton simulated\-localnet snapshot restore <SNAPSHOT_ID>
acton simulated\-localnet snapshot export <SNAPSHOT_ID> \-\-out snapshots/before\-upgrade.json
acton simulated\-localnet snapshot import snapshots/before\-upgrade.json
.fi
.RE
.RE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fBacton help wallet\fR
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fISimulated localnet guide\fR <https://ton\-blockchain.github.io/acton/docs/simulated\-localnet/overview>
.RE
